h each member of their own team.\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. **Calculate the handshakes within each team:**\n   Each player shakes hands once with each of the other three players on their own team. Since there are four players on each team, the number of handshakes within one team is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4 \\times 3}{2} = 6\n   \\]\n   The division by 2 is because each handshake is counted twice (once for each participant). Since there are three teams, the total number of handshakes within all teams is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 6 = 18\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the handshakes between players of different teams:**\n   Each player shakes hands three times with each player on the other two teams. There are 4 players on each team, so each player shakes hands with 8 players from the other two teams (4 players per team times 2 teams), and each handshake is done three times. Therefore, each player shakes hands with other teams:\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 8 \\times 3 = 96\n   \\]\n   Since there are 12 players in total (3 teams of 4 players each), the total number of handshakes between players of different teams is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{12 \\times 96}{2} = 576\n   \\]\n   The division by 2 is because each handshake is counted twice (once for each participant).\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of handshakes:**\n   The total number of handshakes is the sum of the handshakes within teams and the handshakes between different teams:\n   \\[\n   18 + 576 = 594\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of handshakes is \\(\\boxed{594}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{594}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
